WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.323
- Don't have sex in bars.

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:05.487
Just drink, have fun, and go home.

00:00:05.487 --> 00:00:09.154
(upbeat instrumental music)

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.030
- The best way to get a
drink or shot for free

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:16.810
is be someone who comes
in often and tips us well.

00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:18.283
If you treat us well, we treat you well,

00:00:18.283 --> 00:00:19.173
it's really that simple.

00:00:19.173 --> 00:00:20.120
- Be a big tipper.

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:21.460
I always remember people that tip big

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.210
and I always get 'em a
shot or buy 'em a drink.

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:24.560
Learn the bartender's names.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:26.860
Like, get to know them
when it's not super busy.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:27.893
- Make a connection.

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:30.060
We're more likely to
share a drink with them.

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:31.900
The worst way to get a free
drink is to ask for one.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:33.690
- By the way, I can give you other stuff

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:35.220
for free other than free drinks.

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:38.200
A lot of times I will get
you free food or snacks,

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.343
something like french fries.

00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:42.580
- That's a total lie.

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:45.930
Asking for no ice or
less ice does not change

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:47.770
the other ingredients of the drink.

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:49.010
Nothing else changes.

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:51.090
You're literally just getting less ice,

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:52.380
which is exactly what you asked for.

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:54.130
- I don't know, less ice just means

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:55.340
disappointment most of the time.

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:58.260
- It means you get less in the
cup or you get a smaller cup.

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:00.703
Unless you tip and then
that changes everything.

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:05.670
When customers ask for,
like, a stronger drink,

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:08.460
I just put, like, two or
three drops in the straw,

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:10.320
just to make them think it's stronger.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:11.880
It kinda burns the back
their throat real quick.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:13.970
- The amount we put of alcohol will be

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:16.680
the same no matter what you ask.

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:19.730
You can always pay for a
double shot or you can have

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:22.610
the cup full of ice and
then it's less mixer,

00:01:22.610 --> 00:01:25.310
which will make the flavor
of the alcohol stronger.

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:28.460
- Sounds like they want something strong,

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:30.163
but they don't wanna pay for it.

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:32.770
If you want a strong
drink just order a double.

00:01:34.772 --> 00:01:37.467
- This, this is my number one pet peeve.

00:01:37.467 --> 00:01:39.327
"Yes, I see you, you're
there, there's people

00:01:39.327 --> 00:01:41.310
"that are also here
waiting for my attention."

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:42.230
This is not helping your case.

00:01:42.230 --> 00:01:43.980
- When people say, "Oh, just fix me

00:01:44.377 --> 00:01:45.877
"your favorite drink to have."

00:01:46.010 --> 00:01:48.680
No, what I like is not necessarily
what you're gonna like,

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:50.330
not necessarily what your
best friend's gonna like

00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:51.310
or what your mom's gonna like.

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:52.320
Most of the time I'm just
gonna end up giving you

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:53.710
a vodka soda with a splash of cranberry.

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:56.470
- If you wave your cash or snap at me

00:01:56.470 --> 00:01:58.680
or do anything obnoxious, anything that,

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:00.510
like, you as a human
being would find annoying,

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:01.780
you're gonna get less attention.

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:03.870
- If you snap at me,
you're not getting served.

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:05.850
Like, point blank and a period.

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:09.253
- It's always the people
that, like, schmooze you,

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:11.183
those are the worst tippers.

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:14.520
Your compliments and,
like, your love for me

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:15.593
doesn't pay my bills.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:17.860
- The best way to get
a bartender's attention

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:20.663
is to look at them and smile.

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:22.440
It's like, I mean, when you meet somebody

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:23.273
for the first time.

00:02:23.273 --> 00:02:24.800
- The best way is just to
look like you're ready.

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:25.870
Most of the time, bartenders are

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:28.080
standing in their section of the bar

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:29.820
to see who's ready and who's not.

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:32.240
- So we're always looking
for you, don't worry.

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:34.970
If you stand there, waiting, catch my eye.

00:02:34.970 --> 00:02:37.370
Make sure I saw you and then you're good.

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:40.140
- Patience is rewarded behind the bar.

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:40.973
- Wait your turn.

00:02:40.973 --> 00:02:42.170
Don't worry, I will get to you.

00:02:42.170 --> 00:02:44.170
You will get your drink, you'll be fine.

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:47.260
Nobody's gonna say no to, like,

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:49.181
a handshake with something in it.

00:02:49.181 --> 00:02:50.143
- Cash is always king.

00:02:50.143 --> 00:02:51.460
Like, always slip cash.

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:54.050
- If they did a really
bad job and you didn't

00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:56.020
have a lot of fun give ten percent.

00:02:56.020 --> 00:02:58.570
If they were fine and
you were kind of okay

00:02:58.570 --> 00:02:59.560
give fifteen percent.

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:02.113
And if they did a good job
and you had a good time,

00:03:02.170 --> 00:03:03.570
you should give a twenty percent tip.

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:04.590
- It's a decision that you make.

00:03:04.590 --> 00:03:06.603
Twenty percent's a good place to start.

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:10.163
- Do I drink on the job?

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:11.293
No.

00:03:11.293 --> 00:03:12.765
- Yes, always, every single time.

00:03:12.765 --> 00:03:14.310
- I like to call it quality control.

00:03:14.310 --> 00:03:15.890
- Oh my God, you're gonna get me fired.

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:17.970
I used to a lot.

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:19.360
I can finish a whole bottle of Jamison

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:20.290
before I even sell one.

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:21.890
You make more money not, though.

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:23.920
- I just wanna make you happy.

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:25.850
Drink what you wanna drink
and if I can make it,

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:26.726
I'll make it good.

00:03:26.726 --> 00:03:30.393
(upbeat instrumental music)

